��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n�������� ���� ����������� ��� ������ ��� �������������� ���� �������� ��� ���� ��������� ������������ ��� \n���������������������������������������������������� ��������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n�������� ������� ����������� ������ ������ ���� ���� ������������� ������ ���� ���������� ���������� ������� ��� \n��������� ������ ������������� ����� ������� ��� ����� �������� ������ �������� ���� �������� ���� ��������� \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n���� �������� ������������� ��� ��������� �������� �������� ��� ������� ���������� ������ ������� ���� ����� \n�������������������������������������������������������\n�� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n�������� ����� ���� �������� ����������� ����� ��� ������������ ������� ���������������� �� ������� ���������� \n\n��������� ��� ������� �������� ������� ���� ����� ������ ���� ����� ��������� ������ ���� ������� ������ \n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�� �������������� ��������� ��������������� ��� �������������� ��������� ����� ����� �������� ���� \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n���������������\n�� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n���� ��� ������� ����� ������ ������� ������ ����� ������������ ��������������� ���� ���������� ��� ������� \n���������� ��� ������ ������ ����� ����� ������� ����������� ��� ����������� ��� ������ ������������ ������ \n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n������� ����� ��� ������� ����� ����� �������� ������ ������ ��� ��������� ��� ����������� ��� ���� ����������� \n�����������\n�� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n������ ���������� ��� ������� ����� ����������� �������������� ���������� ������� ������������ ����� ������ ���� \n������ �������� ������������������� ������ ���������� �������� ������� �������� ���� ���������� �������� \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n����������������������������������������������������������\n��������� ��� ����������� ��� ���� ������� ��� ��������� ������ ��������� ������ ��� ��������� \n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ��������� ��� ���������� ��������� ������� ������ ���� ������������ ��� ���� ��������� ���������� ��� ������ \n������������� ��� ����������� ��� ����� ���� ���������� ��� ������ ������� ��� ������ ������� ���� ����������� \n����������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |141", "t": "Restoration and Development of Monuments", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION  NO. †*141 \nANSWERED ON 13.02.2023 \n \n \nRESTORATION AND DEVELOPMENT OF MONUMENTS \n \n Will the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state: \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF CULTURE, TOURISM AND DEVELOPMENT OF NORTH EASTERN \nREGION \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n†*141. SHRI DINESH LAL YADAV “NIRAHUA”: \nSHRI C.R. PATIL: \n(a) whether many archaeological monuments located in various States of the country need to \nbe restored and developed; \n(b) \n \nif so, the steps taken/being taken by the Government to restore and develop these \nmonuments along with the details of the schemes to provide funds to State \nArchaeological Departments; \n(c) whether several monuments related to sages in Azamgarh, Uttar Pradesh are being \nproposed to be restored and developed along with the ASI protected sites in Gujarat; \n(d) if so, the time by which it is likely to be done; and \n(e) if not, the reason therefor? \n\n \n \n \n---- \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                                                                                                                             \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*141 FOR 13.02.2023. \n \n(a) \n  & \n  (b) \n   \n \n \n \nArchaeological Survey of India (ASI) has 3696 Centrally Protected Monuments \nin various States of the country. ASI is taking up conservation work of \nmonuments as and when necessary, as per availability of resources.  Upkeep of \nthe monuments is a continuous process.  There is no scheme to provide funds to \nthe State Archaeology Departments by the Government of India. \n      (c) \n       to \n      (e) \nThere are no such monuments protected by ASI in Azamgarh, Uttar Pradesh.  ASI \nhas 205 centrally protected monuments/sites in the State of Gujarat. Conservation \nworks are carried out as per requirement and they are in a good state of \npreservation. \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |142", "t": "Suicides by Daily Wagers", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 142 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 13.02.2023 \n \nSUICIDES BY DAILY WAGERS \n \n*142. SHRI THIRUNAVUKKARASAR SU: \n  \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)whether it is a fact that daily wagers are the largest group among \nthose who have died by suicide during the last few years; \n(b)if so, the details thereof and the number of cases reported in the \ncountry during the last three years, year-wise; \n(c)whether any steps  are being taken by the Government to protect \nthe daily wage earners from suicides and to improve their \nlivelihood; \n(d)if so, the details thereof; and \n(e)if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI BHUPENDER YADAV) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n**                                                   ****** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT  REFERRED TO REPLY TO PART (a) & ( e ) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 142* FOR 13.02.2023 REGARDING “SUICIDES \nBY DAILY WAGERS” RAISED BY SHRI THIRUNAVUKKARASAR SU. \n \n(a) & (b): The profession -wise number of suicides committed by \npeople in the country during 2019 to 2021 is given at Annexure as per \nlatest published data till year 2021 , received from National Crime \nRecords Bureau (NCRB). \n \n(c) &(d): As per the Unorganised Workers‟ Social Security Act, 2008, \nthe Government is mandated to provide Social Security to the workers \nof unorganised sector including daily wage workers by formulating \nsuitable welfare schemes on matters relatin g to (i) life and disability \ncover, (ii) health and maternity benefits, (iii) old age protection and (iv) \nany other benefit as may be determined by the Central Government. \n \nThe Life and Disability cover is provided through Pradhan \nMantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY) and Pradhan Mantri \nSuraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY).  PMJJBY is available to the people in \nthe age group of 18 to 50 years having a bank/post office account who \ngive their consent to join/enable auto debit. Risk coverage under this \nscheme is fo r Rs. 2.00 lakh in case of death of insured, due to any \nreason, at an annual premium of Rs. 436/ - which is to be auto debited \nfrom the subscriber‟s bank/post office account. As on 31.12.2022, a \ntotal of 14.82 crore beneficiaries have been enrolled under th e \nscheme. \nThe Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY) is also \navailable to the people in the age group of 18 to 70 years with a \nbank/post office account who give their consent to join/enable auto \ndebit. The risk coverage under the scheme is for Rs 2.00  lakh in case \nof accidental death or total permanent disability and Rs. 1.00 lakh for \npartial permanent disability; due to accident at a premium of Rs. 20 \nper annum which is to be deducted from the account holder‟s \nbank/post office account through „auto -debit‟.  As on 31.12.2022, a \ntotal of 31.88 crore beneficiaries have been enrolled under the \nscheme. \nThe Ayushman Bharat -Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana \n(ABPMJAY) provides an annual health cover of Rs . 5 lakhs per eligible \nfamily for secondary and tertiary care hospitalization corresponding to \n1949 treatment procedures across 27 specialties. As on 4th \nDecember, 2022, a total of 20.96 crore beneficiaries have been \nprovided with the Ayushman Cards. \n\n \nIn o rder to provide old age protection, the Government of \nIndia launched Pradhan Mantri Shram Yogi Maan -Dhan (PM -SYM) \npension scheme in 2019. It provides monthly pension of Rs.3000/ - after \nattaining the age of 60 years. The workers in the age group of 18 -40 \nyears whose monthly income is Rs. 15000/ - or less and not a member \nof EPFO/ESIC/NPS (Govt. funded) can join the PM -SYM Scheme. Under \nthis scheme 50% monthly contribution is payable by the beneficiary \nand equal matching contribution is paid by the Central Government. As \non 30.01.2023, a total of 49.25 lakh beneficiaries have been enrolled \nunder the scheme. \n \nApart from above, other schemes such as Public \nDistribution System through One Nation One Ration Card scheme \nunder National Food Security Act, Mahatma Gand hi National Rural \nEmployment Guarantee Act, Deen Dayal Upadhyay Gramin Kaushal \nYojana, Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana, Gareeb Kalyan Rojgar Abhiyan, \nMahatma Gandhi Bunkar Bima Yojana, Deen Dayal Antyodaya Yojana, \nPMSVANidhi, Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana  etc. are also \navailable for the unorganised workers including labourers depending \nupon their eligibility criteria. \n \ne-SHRAM portal was launched in August, 2021 with an \nobjective to create National Database of Unorganised Workers (NDUW) \nof the age group of  16-59 years to facilitate delivery of Social Security \nSchemes/Welfare Schemes of the Central and State Governments to \nthe unorganized workers. \n \n(e):  Does not arise. \n  \n\nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO REPLY TO PART (a ) & (b) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 142* FOR 13.02.2023 REGARDING “SUICIDES BY DAILY WAGERS” RAI"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |143", "t": "Support to States for their Capital Expenditure", "head": " \nPosition no. 03 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF ECONOMIC AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *143 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY 13th FEBRUARY, 2023 \n[Magha 24, 1944 (SAKA)] \n \n‘Support to States for their Capital Expenditure’ \n \nNo. *143.  Shri  A. Ganeshamurthi \n      Shri A. Raja  \n  \nWill the MINISTER OF FINANCE be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government has released instalments of tax due to every State from \ndivisible pool to help accelerate their capital expenditure and if so, the details \nthereof including the amount of instalment of tax released to the States out of the \ndivisible pool during each of the last five years, State/ UT-wise;  \n \n(b) the details and the amount of provisional GST compensation yet to be released \nfor the financial year 2021-22, State/UT-wise including Tamil Nadu;  \n \n(c) whether there has been a delay in the release of the said provisional GST \ncompensation to the States, which are reeling under financial stress and if so, the \ndetails thereof and the reasons therefor; and  \n \n(d)     the time by which all dues will be released to the States? \n \n \nAnswer \n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n \nFINANCE MINISTER     (SMT. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a) to (d) : A Statement is placed on the Table of the House. \n**** \n \n  \n\n \nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No. * 143 for answer on \nFebruary 13th, 2023 raised by Shri  A. Ganeshamurthi and Shri A. Raja  \n \n(a) : Yes, Sir.  The amount of tax devolved to the States for the last five years is \ndetailed in Annexure.  \n \n(b) to (d)  : Taking into account ₹ 1.10 lakh crore for the financial year 2020 -21 and ₹ 1.59 \nlakh crore for the financial  year 2021 -22 released to States/UTs as back to back \nloan in lieu of GST Compensation and the regular GST Compensation paid to \nStates as per provisi ons of GST (Compensation to States) Act, 2017, entire \nprovisional GST Compensation dues of States/UTs has been cleared by the Union \nGovernment for the financial year 2020-21 and up to 31.05.2022.  \n \n***  \n  \n\nANNEXURE \nAmount Devolved to the States \n                                                                                                                                             (Rs. Crore) \nSl. \nNo \nState 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \n2022-23  \ntill \nFebruary \n1 Andhra Pradesh 29001.25 32787.03 28242.39 24460.59 35385.83 32703.24 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 9238.79 10436.14 8987.57 10472.58 14643.90 14198.13 \n3 Assam 22301.52 25215.85 21721.44 18629.32 28150.55 25276.96 \n4 Bihar 65083.19 73602.96 63406.33 59861.41 91352.62 81277.42 \n5 Chhattisgarh 20754.83 23458.69 20205.84 20337.54 28570.86 27531.63 \n6 Goa 2544.27 2878.36 2479.85 2296.53 3356.98 3119.17 \n7 Gujarat 207