mended Technology \nUpgradation Fund Scheme (A -TUFS), National Handicraft Development Programme , Comprehensive \nHandicrafts Cluster Devel opment Scheme, Integrated Wool Development Programme etc. catering \nexclusively for promotion and development of textile sector in the country. Exports of Textiles & Apparel \nincluding Handicrafts has increased by 41%, growing from US$ 31,585 million in FY 2 020-21 to        \nUS$ 44,435 million in FY 2021-22. \n \n(d) & (e): In addition to the above schemes, the Government is implementing following schemes \nfor progress of weavers across the country: \n \n1. National Handloom Development Programme; \n2. Raw Material Supply Scheme; \n \nUnder the above schemes, financial assistance is provided to the eligible handloom \nagencies/weavers for raw materials, common infrastructure development, marketing of handloom \nproducts both in domestic and overseas markets, Weavers MUDRA Loans etc.  \n \n**** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |31", "t": "Industries Supported under the Technology Development Fund", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 31 \nANSWERED ON 02.02.2023 \n \nWELFARE SCHEMES FOR DEVELOPMENT OF MINORITY COMMUNITIES \n  \n31. SHRIMATI SUMALATHA AMBAREESH: \n  \n Will the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the total number of the welfare schemes introduced by the Government for the \ndevelopment of minority during the last five years; \n(b) the allocation of funds for each of the said schemes during the said period, year-wise; \n(c) the total number of beneficiaries in each of the said schemes during the said period, year-\nwise; \n(d) whether the Government has received any representation to increase the allocation for the \nwelfare schemes to benefit more people; and \n(e)  if so, the details thereof; \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n  \n(a) The Government has implemented v