ry under the  Pradhan \nMantri Awas Yojana-Urban (PMAY-U); \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the reas ons therefor; \n(c)  the details of measures being taken to bridge the shortfall; and \n(d)  the measures being taken to ensure timely comp letion of \nhouses under PMAY-U? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n \n(a) to (d) Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs ha s been \nimplementing Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Urban (PMAY -U) under \n‘Housing for All’ Mission since June, 2015 by givin g Central \nassistance to implementing agencies through States/  Union \nTerritories (UTs) for providing all-weather pucca h ouses with basic \ncivic amenities  to all eligible urban beneficiaries through four  \n…2/- \n \n\n-2- \nverticals i.e. Beneficiary-led individual house con struction/ \nenhancement (BLC); Affordable Housing in Partnershi p (AHP); ‘In-\nsitu’ Slum Redevelopment (ISSR); and Credit Linked Subsidy \nScheme (CLSS). \n \nBased on the project proposals submitted by States/  UTs, a total of \n122.69 lakh houses were sanctioned till 31.03.2022.  Against the \nsanctioned houses, 107.55 lakh have been grounded f or \nconstruction; of which 68.02 lakh are completed/ de livered to \nbeneficiaries.  \n \nCompletion of projects generally takes 12-36 months  in different \nverticals of the scheme. Around 45 lakh houses have  been \nsanctioned after 31.03.2020. The scheme period has been extended \nup to 31.12.2024 with existing funding pattern and implementation \nmethodology to complete the houses sanctioned till 31.03.2022. \n \nStates/ UTs have been advised to expedite the const ruction of \nsanctioned houses so that all houses are completed within the \nstipulated timeline as per Detailed Project Reports . Ministry \nregularly monitors progress of the scheme through p eriodic review \nmeetings, video-conferences and field visits.  \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED 