 HOUSING AND URBAN \nAFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether as per Gazette Notification No. S.O. 3358 \n(e) dated 18/09/2019, the permission is sought for \ncombined use as Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) \nstation as well as Electric Vehicle Charging (EVC) \nstation; \n(b)  if so, the applicable use of private land conversio n \nfee would be five per cent or twenty five per cent \nof those applicable for petrol pump; and  \n(c)  whether permissions have been granted by DDA \nfor such Stations/Pumps and if so, the number \nthereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n       \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n     (SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n \n(a)  & (b) The Gazette notification no. S.O. 3358 (e) da ted \n18/09/2019 provides that in case the permission is \nsought for combined use as CNG station as well as \nEVC station, the applicable use conversion fee will  be \n25% of those applicable for petrol pump.  \n \n(c) Delhi Development Authority (DDA) has informed that \nso far 23 applications for combined use as CNG \nstation as well as EVC station have been received. Out \nof these, 04 applications were rejected, deficienci es \nhave been noticed in respect of 10 applications and 09 \napplications are under process.  \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |93", "t": "Promotion of Gaming Start-up Ecosystem", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION \nNO. 93\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2023\n \n \nASPIRE IN ANDHRA PRADESH\n \n \n93. \n \nDR. BEESETTI VENKATA SATYAVATHI:\n \n      \n \nDR. SANJEEV KUMAR SINGARI:\n \n      \n \nSHRI KURUVA \nGORANTLA MADHAV:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe current status of projects being incubated under A Scheme for Promotion of Innovation, \nRural Industries and Entrepreneurship (ASPIRE) in Visakhapatnam\n, Rajahmundry, East Godavari, \nChittoor, Krishna and Guntur;\n \n(b) \n \nthe number of beneficiaries under the said scheme;\n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has any pending proposals under the scheme from the State of \nAndhra Pradesh; and\n \n(d) \n \nif so, the details thereof\n?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI \nBHANU PRATAP SINGH VERMA\n)\n \n \n(a)\n:\n \nThe current status of projects being incubated under A Scheme for Promotion of Innovation, \nRural Industries and Entrepreneurship (ASPIRE) in Visakhapatnam, Rajahmundry, East Godavari, \nChittoor, Krishna and Guntur is placed at Annexure.\n \n \n(b)\n:\n \nAs on 31.12.20\n22, 68,761 trainees have been trained under ASPIRE, out of which 16,891 \ntrainees are self\n-\nemployed; 10,399 trainees are employed in nearby units; 41,471 trainees went for \nfurther studies, etc. \n \n \n(c)\n:\n \nNo proposal is pending in the Ministry for setting up of\n \nLBI under ASPIRE in the State of \nAndhra Pradesh. \n \n \n(d)\n:\n \nDoes not arise.\n \n \n \n*****\n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n \n \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \nNo. 93 \nfor answer on 02.02.2023\n \n \nSTATUS OF PROJECTS UNDER \nA SCHEME FOR PROMOTION OF INNOVATION, RURAL INDUSTRIES AND \nENTREPRENEURSHIP (ASPIRE) IN VISAKHAPATNAM, RAJAHMUNDRY, EAST GODAVARI, CHITTOOR, KRISHNA \nAND GUNTUR DISTRICTS OF ANDHRA PRADESH\n \nSr. \nNo.\n \nDistrict\n \nIncubator \nType\n \nImplementing Agency\n \nApproved \nProjec\nt Cost\n \n(in lakh)\n \nGrant Released\n \n(in lakh)\n \nCurrent Status\n \n1.\n \nRajahmundry\n \nLBI\n \nCoir Board, \nRajahmundry, Andhra \nPradesh\n \n100\n \n100\n \nThe LBI has started training.\n \n2.\n \nEast Godavari\n \nLBI\n \nAditya College of \nEngineering & \nTechnology\n \n50\n \n25\n \nThe LBI has started training.\n \n3.\n \nChittoor\n \nTBI\n \nSri Venkateswara College \nof Engineering & \nTechnology\n \n39.98\n \n39.98\n \nThe TBI has successfully \nincubated 06 startups (Tech \nClean, Techno Agri, Compo \nHome, Rural adz, VR Tech, \nEdusala)\n \n4.\n \nKrishna\n \nTBI\n \nDhanekula Institute of \nEngineering &\n \nTechnology\n \n18.75\n \n9.375\n \nThe TBI is under \nimplementation \n \n5.\n \nKrishna\n \nLBI\n \nIndian Institute of \nPlantation & \nManagement, Vijayawada\n \n100\n \n50\n \nThe LBI is under \nimplementation \n \n6.\n \nGuntur\n \nLBI\n \nScience City of Andhra \nPradesh\n \n91.64\n \n45.82\n \nThe LBI is under \nimplementation\n \nTOTAL\n \n400.37\n \n270.175\n \n \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |94", "t": "Allocation of Funds under PMKKKY", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 94\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nAIRLINES FACING FINANCIAL CRISIS\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the number of airlines facing financial crisis during the last three years in\nthe country;\n(b) the details of the aviation services provided by these companies during the\nsaid period;\n(c) whether the Government proposes to provide assistance to such companies\nin the public interest;\n(d) if so, the details thereof; and\n(e) if not, the reasons therefor?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (e): Financial performance of scheduled Indian Airlines for the last 3\nyears is attached as Annexure-I. The losses to the industry were primarily\nbecause of disruption during Covid -19 pandemic across the globe, currency\ndepreciation (USD/INR), high operating cost environment, especially due to\nincrease in ATF prices, increase in crude oil prices in international market,\nVAT, Excise duty and Ukraine - Russia War.\n \nGovernment has taken various steps to facilitate the airlines. The UDAN\nScheme of the Government of India is a game-changer for the aviation\nindustry. The UDAN Scheme, or Ude Desh Ka Aam Nagrik, is a regional\nconnectivity scheme that seeks to make air travel accessible and affordable for\nthe masses. The enhanced fiscal support in the form of VGF (Viable Gap\nFunding), concession on fuel rates, landing/parking charges and the\ninfrastructural development of unserved airports have not only boosted the\noperations of giant airline companies but has also led to the participation of\nregional start-up airlines such as M/s Star Air, M/s IndiaOne Air and M/s\nFlybig. Other measures taken by the Government include:\n94. SHRI RAMCHARAN BOHRA\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\n \ni) The reduction in Value Added Tax (VAT) on Aviation Turbine Fuel (ATF)\nwas taken up with the State Government / Union Territories levying high\nVAT on ATF.\nii) Goods and Services Tax on (GST) rate has been reduced from 18% to 5 %\nfor domestic Maintenance, Repair and Overhaul (MRO) services.\niii) Airports Authority of India (AAI) and other Airport Developers have\ntargeted capital outlay of approximately Rs. 98,000 crore in airport sector in\nthe next five years for expansion and modification of existing terminals, new\nterminals and strengthening of runways, among other activities.\niv) Government has approved Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme\n(ECLGS) to aviation sector. Based on the industry demand, the scope of\nECLGS has been enhanced to provide credit support to these companies upto\n100% of their total credit outstanding (both fund based and non-fund based\noutstanding) as on reference dates, subject to a cap of Rs. 1500 crore per\nborrower, whichever is lower.\n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |95", "t": "Resumption of Delhi-Ambala Passenger Train", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 95 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.02.2023 \n \nRESUMPTION OF DELHI-AMBALA PASSENGER TRAIN \n  \n†* 95.  SHRI NAYAB SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to resume the operation of train \nnumber 64561 (Delhi - Ambala Passenger) which was suspended during \nthe Corona period;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to resume the regular operation of \nthe train in the Parliamentary constituency of Kurukshetra which were \nsuspended during the Corona period; and  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n (SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n(a) to (d)   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n***** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 95 BY SHRI NAYAB SINGH TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON 08.02.2023 REGARDING RESUMPTION OF DELHI -AMBALA \nPASSENGER TRAIN \n \n(a) and (b)  Indian Railways, to contain the spread of COVID -19 \npandemic, had discontinued all regular passengers carrying trains, \nincluding Mail/Express trains, w.e.f 23.03.2020 and only special trains \nwere being operated. Indian Railways have also undertaken \nrationalization of the time table, including rationalization of train \nservices, in a scientific manner with the assistance of IIT -Bombay. The \nexercise has been undertaken inter alia to provide for better passenger \nsafety by creating maintenance corridor blocks, minimizing conflicts in \nexisting time table, generation of additional path for freight traffic and to \nspeed up train services. Ac cordingly, 64561/62 Delhi -Ambala Passenger \n(via Meerut City -Saharanpur) is now being operated between Delhi and \nSaharanpur as 20411/12 Delhi -Saharanpur Express (via Meerut City).  \nSince, November -2021, train services are being operated with \nrationalized time table and presently 09 pairs of Mail/Express are serving \nDelhi-Meerut City-Saharanpur-Ambala section. \n(c) and (d) Indian Railways do not operate train services on \nParliamentary Constituency -wise/State-wise basis as Railway network \nstraddles across Parliamentary Constituency/State boundaries. However, \nDelhi-Panipat-Kurukshetra-Ambala sector is, presently, being served by \n50 pairs of Mail/Express service.  \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |96", "t": "Startups in Space Technology based Business", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 96 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 02, 2023 \n \nREMEDIATION OF LANDFILLS UNDER SBM-U 2.0 \n \nNO. 96. SHRI SATYADEV PACHAURI:  \n \nWill the Minister for HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has proposed for the rem ediation of \nlandfills in the country under Swachh Bharat Missio n–Urban 2.0 \n(SBM-U 2.0); \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government maintains a list of the number of \nlandfills in the country; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof, State/District-wis e, especially in Uttar \nPradesh? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n \n(a) to (d) : SBM-U 2.0 is being implemented with a vision of achieving \n“Garbage Free” status for all cities, which inter alia  involves, \nremediation of all existing landfills/ legacy dumps ites by 2026 for \nwhich Central Financial Assistance is being provide d. As per reports \nreceived from the States, out of 2,955 landfills ac ross the country, \n460 landfills have been remediated. The details of all States along \nwith Uttar Pradesh have been placed in the public d omain at \nhttps://sbmurban.org/swachh-bharat-mission-progess .  \n*****  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |97", "t": "Single Sub-Post Offices", "head": "��\n�\n������������������� �\n��������������������������� �\n�������������� ���� ��\n�\n��� ������ �\n��������������������� ���\n������������������ ��� ��������������� �\n�\n���������� ������������� �\n�\n������������������������� ������ �\n�������������������� �\n�\n���������������������������������������������������������\n����� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������� ��� ���������� ���� �������� ��� ������ ��������� ������� ������������� ���� ����������\n�������������������������������������\n�\n����� ��������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n����� �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������\n�\n������� �\n������������ �������������������� �������������������� �����\n�������������������� �� �\n����������������������� �\n�\n������������ �����������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |98", "t": "Mega Textile Parks", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 98\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nNATIONAL AVIATION UNIVERSITY\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the aims and objectives of National Aviation University;\n(b) whether the Government proposes to set up NAU campuses in other parts\nof the country and if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) whether the Union Government has received any proposal from the\nGovernment of Telangana for setting up of NAU campus at Hyderabad and if\nso, the details thereof including the steps taken in this regard?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a)to (c) The Rajiv Gandhi National Aviation University (RGNAU) has been\nestablished by an Act of Parliament viz. Rajiv Gandhi National Aviation\nUniversity Act, 2013 at Fursatganj Amethi, Uttar Pradesh. The University has\nbeen envisaged as the Premier Institution of higher learning within the\naviation milieu aimed at providing cutting edge aviation professional and\ncritical research to enhance the Aviation Industry in India.\nThe objective of the University is to facilitate and promote aviation studies,\nteaching, training and research in conjunction with the industry to achieve\nexcellence in operations and management of all the sub-sectors within the\naviation industry. The University aims to achieve excellence in the areas of\naviation management, policy, science and technology, aviation environment,\ntraining in the governing fields of safety and security regulations on aviation\nand other related fields.\n \nCurrently, there is no proposal in Government to set up NAU campuses in\nother parts of the country.\n \nA proposal was received from the Government of Telangana in 2018 for\nsetting up RGNAU's campus in Hyderabad. However, the executive Council\n98. DR. G. RANJITH REDDY\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\nof RGNAU did not approve the same.\n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|STARRED   |99", "t": "Redevelopment of Railway Stations in Andhra Pradesh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 99 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.02.2023 \n \nREDEVELOPMENT OF RAILWAY STATIONS IN ANDHRA PRADESH \n*99.  SHRI LAVU SRI KRISHNA DEVARAYALU: \n SHRI BALASHOWRY VALLABHANENI: \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n   \n(a) whether three railway stations in Andhra Pradesh viz. Vizag, \nTirupati and Nellore have been identified for redevelopment, if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n(b) whether any techno -economic feasibility studies have been \nundertaken for these railway stations, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the details of statutory clearances required for the above stations; \nand \n(d) the steps taken by the Railways to get such clearances so far, \nstations-wise? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d ) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 99  BY SHRI LAVU SRI KRISHNA \nDEVARAYALU AND SHRI BALASHOWRY VALLABHANENI TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 08 .02.2023 REGARDING \nREDEVELOPMENT OF RAILWAY STATIONS IN ANDHRA PRADESH \n (a) to (d ): Yes Sir, Vizag (Visakhapatnam), Tirupati and Nellore \nRailway Stations in the state of Andhra Pradesh have been identified \nfor redevelopment. Techno -economic feasibility studies have been \ntaken up for these projects and Detailed Project Reports have  been \nprepared.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n The above projects have been planned for execution in \nEngineering, Procurement and Construction (EPC) mode. The detailed \ndesigns and execution methodology under the EPC contracts are \nprepared by the contractor and based upon the repercussions of the \nplanning and designs, the appropriate clearances are processed which \nis a continuous process. \n \n These three stations are progressing well. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |1", "t": "Expansion of Airport", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 1\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nEXPANSION OF AIRPORT\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to expand the airport network and take\nair travel to the smallest cities in the country;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (c): Ministry of Civil Aviation has launched Regional Connectivity\nScheme (RCS) - UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Nagrik) on 21.10.2016 to stimulate\nregional air connectivity and making air travel affordable to the masses. An\nairport which is included in the awarded routes of UDAN and requires\nupgradation / development for commencement of flight operations, is\ndeveloped under \"Revival/upgradation of unserved and underserved\nairports/heliports/water aerodromes\" Scheme.\n \nAs on 20.01.2023, after four rounds of bidding under UDAN, 459 routes have\ncommenced, operationalizing 72 Airports including 2 Water Aerodrome & 9\nHeliports. More than 2.16 lakh UDAN flights have been operated and over\n1.13 crore passengers have availed the benefits in UDAN flights so far. The\nscheme has been able to provide air connectivity to Tier-2 &Tier-3 cities\nacross the country at affordable airfares and has transformed the way people\ntravel.\n \n \n \n*****\n1. SHRI S. JAGATHRAKSHAKAN\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |10", "t": "Points of Call Status to Airports", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 10\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nFLIGHT DISRUPTIONS DUE TO FOG\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the movement of aircraft were widely affected and the passengers had to face\na lot of difficulties due to low visibility at Darbhanga airport during winter and if so, the\ndetails thereof;\n(b) whether installation of Clear Air Turbulence (CAT-2 ILS) and Aeronautical Ground\nLighting System (AGLS) is underway since 2021 to address the said problem but the said\nwork is not completed till now and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) the time by which the above works are likely to be completed; and\n(d) the details of the action plan of the Government for development of the said airport?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n*****\n*10. SHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR\n be pleased to state:-\n (Shri Jyotiraditya M. Scindia)\n\nStatement in reply to parts (a) to (d) of the Starred (*) Question No. 10 for answer on\n02.02.2023 regarding 'Flight Disruptions due to Fog'.\n \n(a): During the  Winter Schedule of 2022-23 (from 01.12.2022 to 29.01.2023), 64 aircraft\nmovements (Arrival & Departure) got cancelled at Darbhanga airport, due to low\nvisibility conditions.\n \n(b) & (c): Darbhanga Airport is owned and operated by Indian Air Force (IAF) and\nAirports Authority of India (AAI) maintains a Civil Enclave. IAF is responsible for\nmaintenance/ upgradation of airside infrastructure. As informed by IAF, works are in\nprogress for installation of Category II (CAT II) Instrument Landing System (ILS) with\nAeronautical Ground Lighting System (AGLS) as part of Modernization of Airfield\nProject with the probable date of completion as April 2024.\n \n(d): Airports Authority of India (AAI) has taken up strengthening of Runway, taxi track,\napron and construction of runway shoulders, Runway End Safety Area (RESA) and Blast\nPad at Darbhanga airport. \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |100", "t": "Petrol Pumps in Various States", "head": "Source: PPAC  \n \n \nANNEXURE - 2 \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a)&(b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.100 for \n2.2.2023 asked by Shri Naba Kumar Sarania, MP regarding \"Petrol Pumps in Various States\".  \nPSU OMC - District wise number of Retail Outlets as on 1.1.2023 \n \nSR. \nNO. STATE/UT DISTRICT NAME NO. of \nROs OMC \n1 ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR ISLANDS UT NICOBAR 2 IOC \n2 ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR ISLANDS UT NORTH&MIDDLE \nANDAMAN 5 IOC \n3 ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR ISLANDS UT SOUTH ANDAMAN 12 IOC \n  ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR ISLANDS UT \nTOTAL   19   \n4 ANDHRA PRADESH ALLU