he States/UTs \nincluding Maharashtra, West Bengal and Bihar for loss of revenue arising on account of \nimplementation of Goods and Services Tax for five years i.e., from 1st July,2017 to 30th \nJune, 2022. However, due to non -furnishing of final revenue figures, as audited by the \nComptroller and Auditor -General of India by the State, final adjustments could not be \ncalculated and released/recovered to Maharashtra for FY 2021 -22, West Bengal for the \nFY 2017-18 to FY 2021 -22 and Bihar for the FY 2020 -21 to FY 2021 -22. The details of \nGST compensation released to States/ UTs during the last three years are as per \nAnnexure. \n*** \n  \n\n    Annexure \nDetails of GST Compensation released during the Year (FY-Wise) \n \n   \n(Rs. In Crore) \nS.No \nName of State/UT \nFY 2020-21 FY 2021-22 FY 2022-23 \n(1) (2) (3) (4) (5) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 3,527 3,117 4,570 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 6 0 0 \n3 Assam 1,370 1,014 424 \n4 Bihar 4,359 1,945 184 \n5 Chhattisgarh 3,212 1,217 2,439 \n6 Delhi 5,522 6,446 12,817 \n7 Goa 813 911 1,531 \n8 Gujarat 11,335 8,329 7,955 \n9 Haryana 5,066 2,909 2,576 \n10 Himachal Pradesh 1,764 1,168 1,293 \n11 J & K 2,171 893 418 \n12 Jharkhand 1,958 1,526 2,065 \n13 Karnataka 13,789 8,976 20,288 \n14 Kerala 6,721 3,856 7,246 \n15 Madhya Pradesh 5,293 3,095 4,572 \n16 Maharashtra 17,423 17,834 24,121 \n17 Manipur 22 0 0 \n18 Meghalaya 172 163 0 \n19 Mizoram 11 0 0 \n20 Nagaland 14 0 0 \n21 Odisha 4,362 2,465 1,887 \n22 Puducherry 607 329 723 \n23 Punjab 9,694 4,442 7,869 \n24 Rajasthan 5,633 3,746 4,260 \n25 Sikkim 26 9 0 \n26 Tamil Nadu 11,142 6,697 16,215 \n27 Telangana 3,103 2,006 4,062 \n28 Tripura 277 101 0 \n29 Uttar Pradesh 9,324 8,299 11,291 \n30 Uttarakhand 2,496 1,475 2,136 \n31 West Bengal 5,776 4,531 8,228 \n Total 1,36,988 97,500 1,49,168 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |374", "t": "Legal Advice on OBC Quota in Agricultural Universities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE \n DEPARTMENT OF LEGA