s  in different \nverticals of the scheme. Around 45 lakh houses have  been \nsanctioned after 31.03.2020. The scheme period has been extended \nup to 31.12.2024 with existing funding pattern and implementation \nmethodology to complete the houses sanctioned till 31.03.2022. \n \nStates/ UTs have been advised to expedite the const ruction of \nsanctioned houses so that all houses are completed within the \nstipulated timeline as per Detailed Project Reports . Ministry \nregularly monitors progress of the scheme through p eriodic review \nmeetings, video-conferences and field visits.  \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |400", "t": "Anganwadi Centres in Uttar Pradesh", "head": "O.I.H.  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \n STARRED QUESTION NO. 400 \n  ANSWERED ON 28/03/2023 \n \nCOMMENCEMENT OF WORK UNDER NEXT PHASE OF PMAY-G \n*400.  SHRI SANJAY JADHAV:  \nDR. SANGHMITRA MAURYA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government proposes to start the next phase of the Pradhan Mantri Awaas \nYojana-Gramin (PMAY-G);  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the time by which the said work is likely to be started in the   \nvillages in the districts of Parbhani Parliamentary Constituency of Maharashtra and \nBadaun Parliamentary Constituency of Uttar Pradesh;  \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor;  \n(d)  whether the names of the villages under the said Parliamen tary Constituencies have been \nfinalized under the said yojana;  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the time by which the said houses are likely to be allotted \nand if not, the reasons therefor; and  \n(f)  the number of houses to be allotted in the said Parl iamentary Constituencies in the next \nphase during the next three years? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n \n(a) to (f):    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\nSta