5 FOR 06.02.2023  \n  \n Development Sector -wise CSR expenditure (In Rs. Crores) \nS. No Development Sector \n \nFY 2018-19 \n \nFY 2019-20 \n \nFY 2020-21 \n1 Agro Forestry 64.75 67.38 19.24 \n2 Animal Welfare 98.33 106.12 192.71 \n3 Armed Forces, Veterans, War Widows/ \nDependants 90.18 62.04 83.76 \n4 Art And Culture 225.94 933.47 484.68 \n5 Clean Ganga Fund 8.11 6.63 13.39 \n6 Conservation Of Natural Resources 173.55 160.60 90.96 \n7 Education 6,102.18 7,175.85 6,607.64 \n8 Environmental Sustainability 1,367.99 1,470.26 1,029.12 \n9 Gender Equality 51.86 82.93 42.54 \n10 Health Care 3,612.03 4,902.69 7,182.67 \n11 Livelihood Enhancement Projects 907.64 1,077.59 821.16 \n12 Other Central Government Funds 73"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |626", "t": "Declaration of Monuments as Monuments of National Importance in West Bengal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY CULTURE \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.626 \nANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \n \nDECLARATION OF MONUMENTS AS MONUMENTS OF NATIONAL \nIMPORTANCE IN WEST BENGAL \n \n626.  SHRI JAGANNATH SARKAR: \nWill the Minister of Culture be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the district-wise number of monuments or sites declared as monuments of national \nimportance by the Archaeological Survey of India in West Bengal; \n(b) the details of the amount spent on the said monuments or sites during the last three \nyears; \n(c) the year-wise revenue earned by the Government from these monuments during the \nlast three years; \n(d) whether the Government proposes to declare any other monument as a monument of \nnational importance in West Bengal; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof, district-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF CULTURE, TOURISM AND \nDEVELOPMENT OF NORTH EASTERN REGION \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a)  135 monuments and sites are declared to be of national importance in West Bengal. \nDistrict-wise number of monuments and sites is at Annexure. \n(b) Details of the amount spent on conservation, preservation and maintenance of these \nmonuments and  sites during the last three years are given as under: \n                          (Amount in Crore) \nyear Expenditure  \n2019-20 9.68 \n2020-21 8.10 \n2021-22 7.37 \n \n (c)  The  revenue from these monuments on the said monuments or sites during the last \nthree years is given as under: \n                              (Amount in Crore) \nyear Expenditure \n2019-20 3.29 \n2020-21 1.23 \n2021-22 1.65 \n \n(d) \n& \n(e) \nAt present no such proposal is under consideration. \n--- \n\nAnnexure \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED    QUESTION NO. 626 FOR 06.02.2023. \n \nDISTRICT-WISE NUMBER OF MONUMENTS AND SITES OF NATIONAL \nIMPORTANCE IN THE STATE OF WEST BENGAL \n \nSl.No. District Number of Monument / Site  \n1.  Bankura 36 \n2.  Birbhum 05 \n3.  Burdwan 11 \n4.  Cooch Behar 02 \n5.  Darjeeling 02 \n6.  Dinajpur (South) 02 \n7.  Hooghly 11 \n8.  Howrah 01 \n9.  Kolkata 06 \n10.  Malda 21 \n11.  Midanapur 06 \n12.  Murshidabad 22 \n13.  Nadia 02 \n14.  North 24 Parganas 05 \n15.  Purba Medinipur 01 \n16.  Purulia 01 \n17.  South 24 Parganas 01 \n Total 135 \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|11|UNSTARRED |628", "t": "Registered Workers in e-SHRAM Portal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 628 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \n \nREGISTERED WORKERS IN E-SHRAM PORTAL \n \n628.  SHRI P.V. MIDHUN REDDY: \n \n  Will the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)the State-wise number of registered workers on the e -SHRAM portal \nsince its launch; \n(b)whether the Government has taken note that in the unorganised \nsector many people are working beyond the age limit of 60 years; \nand \n(c)if so, the steps taken to ensu re adequate provision of benefits \nlinked to the portal to them? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n(a):  On 26.08.2021, Ministry of Labour &  Employment has \nlaunched e -SHRAM portal, a National Database of the Unorganised \nWorkers aged between 16 -59 seeded with Aadhaar. As on 31.01.2023, \nmore than 28.56 crore unorganised workers have been registered on \nthe portal and the State-wise detail is attached as Annexure. \n(b) & (c): The Government has launched the  Pradhan Mantri Shram \nYogi Maan -dhan (PM -SYM) Scheme in 2019. It is a voluntary and        \nco-contributory scheme for welfare of the unorganised workers. The \nscheme provides a monthly pension of Rs. 3000/- on attaining the age \nof 60 years. The workers in the age group of 18 -40 years whose \nmonthly income is Rs. 15000/ - or less and not a member of \nEPFO/ESIC/NPS (Govt. funded) can join the scheme. Under the scheme, \n50% monthly contribution is payable  by the beneficiary and equal \nmatching contribution is paid by the Central Government. The scheme \nis also linked to e-SHRAM portal. \n*                                                      ****** \n \n \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure referred to in reply to Part (a) of Lok Sa bha Unstarred Question No. 628 for 06.02.2023 \nregarding “Registered Workers in e-SHRAM Portal” raised by SHRI P.V.MIDHUN REDDY \n \nThe state-wise number of registered workers on the e-SHRAM portal as on 31.01.2023 \nState Total Registrations \nUTTAR PRADESH 8,30,04,110 \nBIHAR 2,85,53,787 \nWEST BENGAL 2,57,82,641 \nMADHYA PRADESH 1,68,69,468 \nMAHARASHTRA 1,34,44,317 \nODISHA 1,33,25,936 \nRAJASTHAN 1,27,82,019 \nGUJARAT 91,36,520 \nJHARKHAND 91,36,018 \nTAMIL NADU 83,52,759 \nCHHATTISGARH 82,53,697 \nANDHRA PRADESH 79,07,981 \nKARNATAKA 73,84,000 \nASSAM 69,22,940 \nKERALA 59,03,354 \nPUNJAB 54,95,385 \nHARYANA 52,52,989 \nTELANGANA 40,69,680 \nJAMMU AND KASHMIR 33,67,355 \nDELHI 32,51,071 \nUTTARAKHAND 29,71,660 \nHIMACHAL PRADESH 19,23,013 \nTRIPURA 8,44,264 \nMANIPUR 4,04,682 \nMEGHALAYA 2,86,788 \nNAGALAND 2,18,571 \nPUDUCHERRY 1,76,361 \nCHANDIGARH 1,74,078 